.TH WSPANEL 1 "" "WSPanel" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wspanel \- command line client of the WSPanel REST API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wspanel
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wspanel
talks to a WSPanel panel over its REST API with an API token (created in the
panel under API tokeny): lists sites, starts deploys, reads their state.
.B wspanel login
.I url token
keeps the address and the token in \fI~/.config/wspanel\fR; run
.B wspanel help
for the commands.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Instead of
.BR "wspanel login" :
.TP
.B WSPANEL_URL
The panel's address.
.TP
.B WSPANEL_TOKEN
The API token.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR panel-agent (8)
